  "question": {
    "text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> stone tied at the end of a string <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long is whirled along a vertical circle at a constant speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What will be the tension in the string (in newton) at the bottom-most point?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "52",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Tension at the bottom of the circle,<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
